// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nictus_Nictus_Hunter_Minion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P292674916" "Void Seekers are the lowest rank among the deadly Void Hunter mercenaries, serving mostly as scouts to detect possibly Kheldian activity. They carry a powerful Quantum Array gun specially designed to damage and disrupt Kheldian energy signatures, and have special Nictus fragment implants that protect them from energy attacks."
// GroupDescription :
"P3405360523" "Void Hunters"
// DisplayNames :
"P2240771890" "Void Seeker"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nictus_Nictus_Hunter_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2864815856" "Void Stalkers are drawn from the ranks of Void Seekers who have proven their cunning and viciousness in battle. Extra training, more powerful Quantum Array weaponry, and additional Nictus fragment implants transform them into something dangerous to most heroes and deadly to Kheldians."
// DisplayNames :
"P194758577" "Void Stalker"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nictus_Nictus_Hunter_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2853576806" "Void Slayers are the deadliest operatives the Void Hunter mercenaries have at their disposal. They carry the most powerful Quantum Array weapons available and have dozens of Nictus fragment implants, allowing them to destroy a Kheldian with little risk to themselves."
// DisplayNames :
"P408941834" "Void Slayer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nictus_Bright_Nova 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P371221034" "Every Kheldian energy being retains the patterns of its past hosts, and can use these patterns to transform itself and its current host into an energy-based duplicate of that creature, gaining new abilities in the process. The Bright Nova form is patterned off of a race called the Mefnanim that lived in the energy-charged upper atmosphere of a gas giant planet. The Bright Nova form retains the ability fly and to shape and project energy bolts of incredible power."
// DisplayNames :
"P2940900550" "Bright Nova"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nictus_Dark_Nova 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P162251635" "Every Kheldian energy being retains the patterns of its past hosts, and can use these patterns to transform itself and its current host into an energy-based duplicate of that creature, gaining new abilities in the process. The Dark Nova form is patterned off of a race called the Hulnanim that lived in the lightless depths of a gas giant planet. The Dark Nova form retains the ability to fly and to shape and project dark energy bolts of incredible power."
// DisplayNames :
"P3668171698" "Dark Nova"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nictus_White_Dwarf 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1163313974" "Every Kheldian energy being retains the patterns of its past hosts, and can use these patterns to transform itself and its current host into an energy-based duplicate of that creature, gaining new abilities in the process. The White Dwarf form is patterned off of a race called the Kurukt that lived on the surface of a neutron star. The White Dwarf form retains the incredible physical resilience of the Kurukt, as well as the ability to channel energy into powerful melee attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P1436347276" "White Dwarf"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nictus_Dark_Dwarf 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3942867904" "Every Kheldian energy being retains the patterns of its past hosts, and can use these patterns to transform itself and its current host into an energy-based duplicate of that creature, gaining new abilities in the process. The Dark Dwarf form is patterned off of a race called the Ruktur that lived on the surface of a pulsar. The Dark Dwarf form retains the incredible physical resilience of the Ruktur, as well as the ability to channel energy into powerful melee attacks."
// DisplayNames :
"P4110272813" "Dark Dwarf"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nictus_Shadow_Crystal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P434155126" "These unearthly crystals grow form a Shadow Seed, a hardened physical form created when several Nictus fuse together and solidify themselves. Shadow Cysts project a field that allows Nictus to survive for extended periods without a host even on a planet's surface. The Cysts also act like wormholes, allowing Nictus to travel instantly from one cyst to another, even across interstellar distances. If allowed to grow in the right conditions, a Shadow Cyst can flood a world with Nictus."
// DisplayClassName :
// DisplayNames :
"P3126413666" "Shadow Cyst Crystal"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nictus_Crystal_Nictus_Entity_Minion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1841177338" "These free-floating Nictus have been drawn to Earth from somewhere in the Cosmos, bridging the distance through a Shadow Cyst. They have not yet joined with or possessed a host, and normally could not survive on a planet's surface for long. However, the dark energies of the Shadow Cyst sustain them, allowing them to hunt for hosts on their own."
// DisplayNames :
"P639955794" "Lesser Unbound Nictus"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nictus_Crystal_Nictus_Entity_Lt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3737211635" "Unbound Nictus"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Nictus_Crystal_Nictus_Entity_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3919943333" "Greater Unbound Nictus"

